IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 20 (APPEALS FROM TRIBUNALS AND CASE STATED), rules 1 to 7.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` unless it says otherwise.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes in its own words.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a definition that "means", a flat negative, a
--                condition introduced by "if", "where", "unless", "only if", "when" or "upon", or a
--                period the text fixes for itself and the act falls outside it).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent, the list is "includes", a term is
--                undefined, the answer is in a provision outside the sources, or the grant is limited
--                by its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc5)".
--
-- THE LAST DAY OF A PERIOD is never counted here: O 3 r 3 counts it (PLAN.md seam S-T1) and the answer
-- is the INPUT `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.  Each period is stated once, as a `Period`
-- constant named for its rule.
--
-- THE BORROWED FACTS are inputs named for the provision that answers them: `o 19 r 41 ...`, `o 19 r 7 ...`,
-- `o 9 r 1 ...` and the keel's own functions.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 20 -- Appeals from tribunals and case stated`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- scope of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 20 r 1(1) kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal`
    `o 20 r 1(1)(b) an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated to the General Division`
    `o 20 r 1(1) another kind of proceeding`

-- "Subject to ... any written law" is not threaded as an input (NOTES.md, Reading a result).  Paragraph (2)
-- is a flat negative about an appeal from a State Court; (1)(a) has its own exception for Order 19, Rule 41,
-- which is another part's answer and so an input.
-- src:2879 | 1. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and any written law, this Order applies to — ( a )
-- src:2880 | every appeal against the decision of a tribunal (except as otherwise provided in Order 19, Rule 41); and
-- src:2881 | ( b )
-- src:2882 | every application for a case to be stated or application by way of case stated to the General Division,
-- src:2883 | where such an appeal or application is provided by the written law.
-- src:2884 | (2) This Order does not apply to an appeal from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act.
@ref O 20 r 1 (src:2879-2884)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 20 r 1(1) kind of proceeding`
      `the appeal or application is provided by the written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 19 r 41 the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appeal is from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Order does not apply to an appeal from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act."
        IF kind EQUALS `o 20 r 1(1) another kind of proceeding`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this Order applies to — ( a ) every appeal against the decision of a tribunal"; (b) every application for a case to be stated
        IF NOT `the appeal or application is provided by the written law`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where such an appeal or application is provided by the written law"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` AND `o 19 r 41 the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except as otherwise provided in Order 19, Rule 41"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 20 r 1(1)(a) an appeal against the decision of a tribunal` AND `o 19 r 41 the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether Order 19, Rule 41 provides for this appeal is that Rule's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Documents that are part of the "record of proceedings".
DECLARE `o 20 r 2 kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `o 20 r 2 written grounds of decision`
    `o 20 r 2 record of evidence or notes of arguments taken`
    `o 20 r 2 affidavit or statutory declaration filed`
    `o 20 r 2 submissions`
    `o 20 r 2 any other document tendered`

-- "record of proceedings" MEANS the listed documents "in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal".
-- A closed definition: a document that is not in respect of those proceedings is outside it.
-- src:2886 | 2. In this Order — “record of proceedings” means any written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments taken, the affidavits or statutory declarations filed, as well as the submissions and any other documents tendered in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal;
@ref O 20 r 2 term record of proceedings (src:2886-2886)
GIVEN document IS A `o 20 r 2 kind of document`
      `it is in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` MEANS
    IF `it is in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“record of proceedings” means any written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments taken, the affidavits or statutory declarations filed, as well as the submissions and any other documents tendered in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal"

-- "tribunal" INCLUDES any authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under any
-- written law, BUT NOT any Court.  Court: flat no.  Authorised body: yes.  Anything else: list not closed.
-- src:2887 | “tribunal” includes any authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under any written law but not any Court.
@ref O 20 r 2 term tribunal (src:2887-2887)
GIVEN `it is an authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a Court`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not any Court"
        IF `it is an authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under a written law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): “tribunal” includes ... and the list is not closed

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- bringing of the appeal or application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2889 | 3. —(1) An appeal against the decision of a tribunal or an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated must be by way of an originating application supported by an affidavit. (2) Subject to any other written law, the originating application and supporting affidavit must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the matter within 14 days after the tribunal’s decision.
@ref O 20 r 3(1) (src:2889-2889)
GIVEN `it is brought by way of an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires` MEANS
    IF `it is brought by way of an originating application` AND `the originating application is supported by an affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be by way of an originating application supported by an affidavit"

`o 20 r 3(2) the period for filing and serving the originating application and the supporting affidavit` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- The anchor is "the tribunal's decision"; the last day is O 3 r 3's answer (an input).
-- src:2889 | 3. —(1) An appeal against the decision of a tribunal or an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated must be by way of an originating application supported by an affidavit. (2) Subject to any other written law, the originating application and supporting affidavit must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the matter within 14 days after the tribunal’s decision.
@ref O 20 r 3(2) (src:2889-2889)
GIVEN `the date the originating application and the affidavit are filed` IS A DATE
      `the date they are served on all parties who have an interest in the matter` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the originating application and the affidavit are filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
       AND `the date they are served on all parties who have an interest in the matter` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the matter within 14 days after the tribunal’s decision" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- src:2889 | 3. —(1) An appeal against the decision of a tribunal or an application for a case to be stated or an application by way of case stated must be by way of an originating application supported by an affidavit. (2) Subject to any other written law, the originating application and supporting affidavit must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the matter within 14 days after the tribunal’s decision.
@ref O 20 r 3(2) (src:2889-2889)
GIVEN `the persons served include all the parties who have an interest in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are served on every interested party` MEANS
    IF `the persons served include all the parties who have an interest in the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the matter"

-- src:2890 | (3) The affidavit must state all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application, the questions of fact or law to be determined and the orders that are sought before the Court.
@ref O 20 r 3(3) (src:2890-2890)
GIVEN `it states all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the questions of fact or law to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the orders that are sought before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` MEANS
    IF `it states all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application`
       AND `it states the questions of fact or law to be determined`
       AND `it states the orders that are sought before the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The affidavit must state all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application, the questions of fact or law to be determined and the orders that are sought before the Court."

-- The duty to include the record exists "if that is available and is necessary".
