@ref O 20 r 3(4) (src:2891-2891)
GIVEN `the record of proceedings is available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record of proceedings is necessary for the appeal or the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the record of proceedings is available` AND `the record of proceedings is necessary for the appeal or the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that is available and is necessary for the appeal or the application"

`o 20 r 3(5) the period for the affidavit in reply` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 21
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2892 | (5) The parties who have been served in paragraph (2) must file and serve an affidavit in reply, if necessary, within 21 days after service.
